---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../components/editorial/SectionLabel.astro';
import MediaFrame from '../components/editorial/MediaFrame.astro';
import OperatingDiagram from '../components/editorial/OperatingDiagram.astro';
import { media } from '../data/media';
import { mediaManifest } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout title="What is an Employer of Record? | Trustora" description="A plain-language guide to Employer of Record services: what an EoR does, what your company keeps, and what to ask before you hire globally." currentPath="/what-is-eor/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="measure page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-copy"><SectionLabel>EoR 101</SectionLabel><h1>What is an Employer of Record?</h1><p>In plain language: an EoR gives a company a local employment layer in a country where it does not yet have its own entity. For specialist teams, that layer can sit beside the expertise needed to move the work forward.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/eor/">See the EoR path <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="page-hero-note">A useful starting point for founders, people leaders, and operators asking whether an EoR fits the next hire.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure split-argument"><h2>Think of it as the employment layer between ambition and local reality.</h2><div class="prose"><p>Your company still directs the work, manages performance, and builds the relationship with the employee. The EoR is the local employer named in the employment arrangement, coordinating the country-specific employment administration around that person.</p><p>That commonly includes contract coordination, payroll, statutory contributions, benefits administration, leave, onboarding, and offboarding. The exact responsibilities depend on the country, the agreement, and the service model.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel light>How the model works</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Three relationships. One clearer map.</h2></div><p>Good EoR work makes responsibilities visible to the company, the employee, and the local employment partner.</p></div><div class="process-map"><div class="process-step"><span class="step-no">01 / YOUR COMPANY</span><h3>Owns the work</h3><p>You set direction, manage the day-to-day, and define what success looks like.</p></div><div class="process-step"><span class="step-no">02 / TRUSTORA</span><h3>Coordinates employment</h3><p>We help administer the local employment relationship and keep the operating details joined up.</p></div><div class="process-step"><span class="step-no">03 / THE EMPLOYEE</span><h3>Gets a clear experience</h3><p>The person knows who employs them, how pay and leave work, and where to ask a question.</p></div><div class="process-step"><span class="step-no">04 / THE COUNTRY</span><h3>Sets the context</h3><p>Local employment, tax, benefits, and worker-protection rules shape the answer.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>Operating diagram</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">A good EoR makes the boundary visible.</h2></div><p>Use the diagram to start the conversation. Then test every handoff against the country, agreement, role, and facts.</p></div><OperatingDiagram kind="eor" /></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure story-grid"><MediaFrame src={media['lab-instrument-research']} alt={mediaManifest['lab-instrument-research'].alt} caption="An EoR model is a shared employment layer around a real role, team, and local context." credit={mediaManifest['lab-instrument-research'].credit} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 55vw" /><div class="story-copy"><SectionLabel>The honest version</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">EoR reduces friction. It does not erase responsibility.</h2><p>Your company still needs to make good decisions about the role, the working relationship, the offer, and the team. Payroll outsourcing does not automatically transfer every employer obligation, and worker classification still depends on the facts and the applicable rules.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/insights/the-trust-layer-in-global-employment/">Read about the trust layer <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section orange-field"><div class="measure intro-slab"><div><SectionLabel light>Next question</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Would an EoR fit your next hire?</h2></div><div class="intro-body"><p>Start with the country, the role, and the timing. We will help you understand the decision—not rush you into a package.</p><a class="button button-light" href="/contact/">Talk to Trustora <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</Layout>
